 "response": "Gikistu's budget is now **$3098K**.\n\n**Which records count**\n- Only Finance Office records change the budget. Every PMO, Engineering, Sales, Operations, Legal, Marketing, Facilities and Vendor message was ignored.\n- Finance Office notes that aren't budget changes (room moves, invoice batches, reminders) were also ignored.\n\n**Withdrawal chains**\n- An update stays out only if the withdrawal that targets it is still in effect.\n- **#0003 is out.** Its chain is #0694 \u2192 #0535 \u2192 #0435 \u2192 #0357 \u2192 #0206 \u2192 #0202 \u2192 #0145 \u2192 #0011 \u2192 #0005 \u2192 #0003. Each link cancels the one before it, so #0005 ends up in effect and #0003 is withdrawn.\n- **#0002 stays in.** Its chain is #0843 \u2192 #0754 \u2192 #0019 \u2192 #0008, which leaves #0008 cancelled.\n- **#0013 stays in** (via #0660 \u2192 #0274 \u2192 #0028 \u2192 #0023).\n- **#0036 stays in** (via #0964 \u2192 \u2026 \u2192 #0067).\n- **#0582 is out** (via #0898 \u2192 #0862 \u2192 #0787).\n- **#0050 is out** (via #1556 \u2192 #1554 \u2192 #0053).\n- About 120 budget updates are withdrawn in total.\n\n**Calculation**\n- Starting from $2070K (#0001), I applied every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease once, in record order.\n- The last change is #1600 (+$130K), which takes the total from $2968K to $3098K.\n- I did not run a second, independent check of the arithmetic.\n\nANSWER: $3098K",
